      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ZENITH STRIDE (8) was terrific in his comeback win last week, racing three wide without cover before scoring by 2.3m at this circuit and distance. That was his first outing for the best part of three years so the hitout should have done him the world of good. Sticking with him. LOTUS LOUISE (11) has nearly 5m to make up on Zenith Stride through their last clash but he is better than that. Had enough speed to lead from wide and win here three back so is good enough with his A-game. EZRA KAI (6) has been close-up in two outings here since switching to Luke McCarthy and could be hitting his peak now. SUNNY GEE (10) will find this easier than last week's attempt and was solid when placed behind Zenith Stride prior so is worth including.",
